import kotlin.Boolean;

-- v14 -> v15: an event no longer closes; it stays open until its photos are deleted (capability `event-lifetime`). The
-- membership learns three more of the event's facts, each from the event's details:
--
--   openUntil       until when the event stays open — its range end, or the date the host chose for an event created
--                   after its end. NULL until the details first carry it.
--   membersWaiting  how many present members are still sharing — the waiting line. NULL beside counts recorded
--                   before it, which then fall back to active minus settled.
--   deleted         the server confirmed the event's photos are deleted. The membership stays, shown as over; the app
--                   never leaves on its own. Every existing row is a membership whose event was not known deleted.
ALTER TABLE membership ADD COLUMN openUntil TEXT;
ALTER TABLE membership ADD COLUMN membersWaiting INTEGER;
ALTER TABLE membership ADD COLUMN deleted INTEGER AS Boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
